The bundle's restart script waits for the application to exit, with no limit

The script quit an application through LaunchServices, then polled
LaunchServices ten times a second and gave up after a fixed number of
seconds, both while the old process exited and while the new one
started. A slow quit was reported as a failure, and the poll interval
and the limit were numbers nobody measured. The script now reads the
process id LaunchServices reports, registers the wait in the machine's
register of open waits (`stado waits open --kind proces`), blocks on
`caffeinate -w` until exactly that process has exited, and closes the
registration. `open` returns once LaunchServices has launched the
bundle, so the launch is checked once and refused by name when no
process is listed. The option that set the limit is removed: no caller
passed it. Every refusal names what failed; usage goes to standard
error.

